{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof of Erdős's 1947 theorem that for any n ≥ 2 distinct interpolation nodes in [-1, 1] the smallest of the n + 1 local maxima of the Lebesgue function Σ|ℓₖ| (over the gaps between consecutive nodes and the endpoints ±1) is less than √n.",
